# Local test environment for the live-HTTP OCS contract tests.
#
# Copy to `.env.testing` and fill in real values. `.env*` is gitignored
# (see .gitignore), so credentials are never committed.
#
# These credentials belong to THIS project's lab only: Compose project `pettycash-lab`,
# served on http://localhost:8081 (see ~/projects/nextcloud-lab/README.md). The PTS lab is a
# separate Nextcloud with a separate database, so a user minted there does not exist here.
#
# `~/projects/nextcloud-lab/bin/lab pettycash up` creates the user, mints the token and
# prints it. To do it by hand:
#   scripts/dev/occ user:add --password-from-env --display-name "Employee One" employee1
#   NC_PASS='<password>' scripts/dev/in-container -e NC_PASS='<password>' \
#     php /var/www/html/occ user:auth-tokens:add --password-from-env \
#       --name pettycash-contract-tests employee1
# The generated token is printed on the line after "app password:".
#
# `--password-from-env` reads NC_PASS from the environment (verified against
# `occ user:auth-tokens:add --help` in Nextcloud 34). Without it the token is minted with
# limited capabilities and any operation requiring the login password fails.

# Nextcloud user the contract tests authenticate as.
PETTYCASH_TEST_USER=employee1

# App password / token for PETTYCASH_TEST_USER.
PETTYCASH_TEST_PASSWORD=

# Base URL of the running Nextcloud, as seen from inside the container.
#
# `localhost`, not `localhost:8081`, and that is correct rather than stale: the contract
# tests are executed by `scripts/dev/phpunit` INSIDE the lab's container (there is no host
# PHP in this project), where Nextcloud answers on port 80 of its own loopback. The
# published port 8081 is the host-side mapping and is not reachable from in there.
# The host-side port matters only for Playwright, which runs on the host — see
# playwright.config.ts.
PETTYCASH_TEST_BASE_URL=http://localhost
